<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38158" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανα-φέρω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαμφέρω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανοίσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			: aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήνεγκα</span>:—<i>throw back
				upon</i>: hence, <i>ascribe, refer,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τι θεοῖς τούτων μοῖραν ἐπαμφέρετε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sol.
					11.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι εἴς τινα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1080
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				434e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				5.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				27.49
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					680d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι αἴτιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					196a13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὸ τέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VM</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			 (v.l.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινα,</span> of an
			analogous case, ib. <i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλιν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					3.33
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὶ ὑπέρ τινος,</span> Lat.
				<i>referre alicui de re,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.4.14
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανενεχθεισῶν τῶν συνθηκῶν εἰς τὴν
					Ῥώμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.17.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> intr. in 
				Act.
			, <i>rise</i> or <i>be referred</i> to a cause, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					219c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>put into the account,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				41.20
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1607a7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bring back a message,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.2.21
			</span></i> (
				Act.
			 with 
				Med.
			 as v.l.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Art.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>vomit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>recover consciousness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανενέγκαντες θνῄσκουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Coac.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			 (unless =
			<i>sigh,</i> cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναφέρω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of disease,
				<i>abate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>rise,</i> as an exhalation, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				5.2
			</span></i>; as stars or the sun, <i><span class="en">
				Gem.
				7.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.19e
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				735a
			</span></i>; esp. in Astrol., <i>occupy the position following a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				115
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>move in counter revolution,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				96d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> Rhet.,
				<i>repeat</i> a word (cf. sq.), <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				59
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				268
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				40
			</span></i>.</div>
